<spell-notebook "emoji theming">
	<header level="1">
		Emoji
		<header>An emoji is a glyph used to represent something else.</>
	</>
	<emoji-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-emoji-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region, `:root`), or on
			the emoji's box through `::part(emoji)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through a
			private alias, so nothing inside blocks them.

			- `--ui-emoji-font-family` picks the emoji font.
			- `--ui-emoji-size-small` / `-large` / `-big` are the size ratios.
			- Class-grammar `medium` is Fomantic's 3em emoji (fixed, not a token): the element treats `medium` as the default
			  size.
			- Never set the `--_ui-*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			/* every emoji on the page */
			:root {
			  --ui-emoji-font-family: "Noto Color Emoji", sans-serif;
			}
			/* one region */
			.reactions {
			  --ui-emoji-size-large: 4;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-emoji" playground>
				<p>
					<ui-emoji name="grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes"></>
					<ui-emoji name="face_with_tears_of_joy"></>
					<ui-emoji name="thumbs_up"></>
					<ui-emoji name="red_heart"></>
					<ui-emoji name="sun"></>
					<ui-emoji name="flag_united_states"></>
					<ui-emoji name="keycap_1"></>
					<ui-emoji name="woman_technologist"></>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			No theme restyles emoji. Fomantic's `joypixels` theme swaps its image set, which we don't have (image emoji
			sets: I1); to change the look, point `--ui-emoji-font-family` at another emoji font.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
